d with direct configuration and runtime evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed coherently on both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service, configuration, and synchronization were captured and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot observations.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-service probe is unsupported because these Alpine nodes do not use systemd; direct OpenRC status and synchronization checks nevertheless cover the relevant chronyd health.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory the retained pre-change configuration backup files, so their final presence is inferred from their creation and the absence of a cleanup command; these are reasonable rollback artifacts and were not treated as unnecessary mutations."]}
